================================================================================
  TCG API DOCUMENTATION
  Project-X Backend
  Last Updated: 2026-05-02
================================================================================

BASE URL
--------
  All TCG routes are prefixed with:
  /v1/api/tcg

  The TCG external service base URL is sourced from the environment variable:
    TCG_URL  (e.g. http://localhost:5000)

================================================================================
  ENDPOINT 1 — TCG Login
================================================================================

  Method  : POST
  Route   : /v1/api/tcg/login
  Full URL: {{HOST}}/v1/api/tcg/login
  Access  : Public (no auth required)

  Description:
    Authenticates against the external TCG service using email and password.
    On success, extracts the JWT token from the TCG response and writes it
    to the frontend .env file as VITE_TCG_TOKEN. Also returns the token in
    the API response.

  ── REQUEST ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  Headers:
    Content-Type: application/json

  Body (JSON):
    {
      "email"    : "lalitkumar709086@gmail.com",   // string, required
      "password" : "StrongPass@123"                 // string, required
    }

  Field Validation:
    • email    — must be a non-empty string
    • password — must be a non-empty string
    • Both fields are required; missing either returns 400

  ── RESPONSES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  200 OK — Login successful, token written to frontend .env
    {
      "success": true,
      "message": "Logged in successfully. Token saved to frontend .env.",
      "token"  : "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..."
    }

  400 Bad Request — Missing email or password
    {
      "success": false,
      "message": "Email and password are required."
    }

  500 Internal Server Error — TCG_URL not set in environment
    {
      "success": false,
      "message": "TCG_URL is not configured in the environment."
    }

  502 Bad Gateway — TCG API responded but token was absent
    {
      "success": false,
      "message": "TCG API did not return a token."
    }

  4xx/5xx (proxied) — TCG API returned an error
    {
      "success": false,
      "message": "TCG API returned an error.",
      "error"  : { ...tcg_error_payload... }
    }

  500 Internal Server Error — Unexpected server-side failure
    {
      "success": false,
      "message": "Internal server error while logging in to TCG."
    }

  ── SIDE EFFECT ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  On success the controller reads the file:
    frontend/.env

  and upserts the following line:
    VITE_TCG_TOKEN=<jwt_token>

  If the key already exists it is replaced in-place.
  If it does not exist it is appended at the end of the file.

  ── EXAMPLE cURL ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/v1/api/tcg/login \
       -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
       -d '{"email":"lalitkumar709086@gmail.com","password":"StrongPass@123"}'

  ── EXAMPLE AXIOS (frontend) ───────────────────────────────────────────────

  const response = await axios.post('/v1/api/tcg/login', {
    email   : 'lalitkumar709086@gmail.com',
    password: 'StrongPass@123',
  });
  console.log(response.data.token);

================================================================================
  ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES USED
================================================================================

  back-end/.env
  ┌──────────────┬────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Variable     │ Description                                            │
  ├──────────────┼────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ TCG_URL      │ Base URL of the external TCG service                   │
  │ TCG_TOKEN    │ (Optional) Last known token stored in backend .env     │
  └──────────────┴────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

  frontend/.env  (written by the controller)
  ┌────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
  │ Variable       │ Description                                          │
  ├────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
  │ VITE_TCG_TOKEN │ JWT token obtained from the last successful TCG login│
  └────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

================================================================================
  FILE STRUCTURE
================================================================================

  back-end/
  ├── controllers/
  │   └── TCGControllers.js   ← tcgLogin controller function
  ├── routes/
  │   └── tcg.js              ← POST /login route
  └── app.js                  ← mounts /v1/api/tcg → tcg router

================================================================================
  NOTES
================================================================================

  • The controller uses axios to call the TCG external API.
    Make sure axios is installed:  npm install axios

  • Writing to frontend/.env at runtime is intended for development / internal
    tooling use.  In production consider using a secrets manager instead.

  • The TCG JWT token expires (check the exp claim). Re-run the login endpoint
    to refresh the token before it expires.

